  "metadata": {
    "title": "Why traffic can stop without a blocked road",
    "caption": "No accident or roadworks were needed in this controlled experiment: 22 cars on a circular track developed stop-and-go traffic.\n\nIn dense traffic, small speed changes can sometimes grow. Cars move forward through the slow patch while the congestion pattern moves backward. Accidents and bottlenecks also cause jams.\n\nOriginal explanatory animation, experiment reconstruction and synthetic narration.",
